.TH POLL 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
poll \- wait for file descriptor events
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <poll.h>
.PP
.BI "int poll(struct pollfd* " descriptors ", nfds_t " count ", int " timeout ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Waits for events on an array of
.I count
Linux x86\-64 pollfd records.
The timeout is in milliseconds; zero returns immediately and \-1 waits
indefinitely. The kernel writes the result events in each record. A negative
descriptor is ignored.
.PP
Each Crunch
.B struct pollfd
contains
.BR fd ,
.BR events_low ,
.BR events_high ,
.BR revents_low ,
and
.BR revents_high .
The last four are bytes in little\-endian order. Set the event bytes to
.B (byte)(flags & 255)
and
.BR "(byte)((flags >> 8) & 255)" ;
combine the result bytes as
.BR "(revents_low & 255) | ((revents_high & 255) << 8)" .
The header defines
.BR POLLIN ,
.BR POLLPRI ,
.BR POLLOUT ,
.BR POLLERR ,
.BR POLLHUP ,
.BR POLLNVAL ,
.BR POLLRDNORM ,
.BR POLLRDBAND ,
.BR POLLWRNORM ,
.BR POLLWRBAND ,
and
.BR POLLRDHUP .
Error, hangup, and invalid\-descriptor events may be returned even if not
requested.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of records with nonzero result events, zero on timeout,
or \-1 with
.B errno
set on failure. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH ERRORS
Include
.BR <errno.h> .
Errors include
.BR EFAULT ,
.BR EINTR ,
.BR EINVAL ,
and
.BR ENOMEM .
.SH NOTES
This is the Linux poll syscall, not a libc cancellation wrapper. Crunch errno
is process\-wide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR select (3crunch),
.BR pipe (3crunch),
.BR poll (2)
